; a rotation matrix R(θ) rotates a vector by angle θ
; in 2D: [[cos θ, -sin θ], [sin θ, cos θ]]
; in 3D axis-aligned: Rx, Ry, Rz (rotate in YZ, XZ, XY planes)
; in 3D arbitrary axis u: Rodrigues formula
; R = I·cosθ + (1-cosθ)·(u⊗u) + sinθ·[u]×
; equivalently: v_rot = v·cosθ + (u×v)·sinθ + u·(u·v)·(1-cosθ)
; implemented as rot3d.tantra using vec-cross inline
; in n-D: a plane of rotation is chosen, same cos/sin structure
; orthogonal: R^T = R^-1, det(R) = 1
; composition: R(θ1+θ2) = R(θ1)·R(θ2)
; in kinematic chains: R_world = R_0 · R_1 · ... · R_{n-1}
; propagated via fk-ndof.tantra (frame reduce over krama joints)

(mantra rotation-matrix
  (karma geometry-varga)
  (swarupa matrix transform orthogonal)
  (yukta kona aayaama)
  (kriya vector)
  (phala direction)
  (pratipaksha rotation-matrix))
